    interpretation:
      '{0} has exactly two master-detail parents ({1} and {2}) — the structural signature of a many-to-many junction. This is the structural pattern only; the object may still carry its own fields, automation, and business data. Because both relationships are master-detail, deleting a record of EITHER parent cascade-deletes the junction records, and the object is necessarily Controlled by Parent (a master-detail invariant, inferred from the relationship type, not read from this object\'s sharing model); record access is gated by both masters. This names the structural pattern, not a proven pure-connector design intent, and Controlled by Parent is derived from the two master-detail edges rather than read from the object\'s sharingModel; which parent is primary and whether the junction is reparentable are not determinable offline, and how many junction records exist under a given parent is a live-plane question.',
